# Fedora Everything netinstall ISOs scripts/build-iso.sh accepts as input.
# The input ISO's SHA256 must match a line here, or the build stops, so every
# Perihelion ISO is built from a known, unmodified Fedora installer.
#
# Format: <name> <sha256> <url>
# The last line is the default for --download.
#
# To add a release: download it from fedoraproject.org, check it against
# Fedora's GPG-signed CHECKSUM file (https://fedoraproject.org/security),
# then add a line. Replace the Beta line once Fedora 45 is final.
#
# 45-beta-1.3: SHA256 as published on https://fedoraproject.org/misc/beta/
# (2026-11-01). Not yet cross-checked against the signed CHECKSUM file.
45-beta-1.3 5d5a7592e6759c37367ac3ef93212307f484c6ca8f5fb6a4c368efa59ecdaf00 https://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/releases/test/45_Beta/Everything/x86_64/iso/Fedora-Everything-netinst-x86_64-45_Beta-1.3.iso
